WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.214 --> 00:00:09.134
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:37.954
AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

3
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.094
You suffered as well.
So. we'll make them pay.

4
00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:56.431
I appreciate the chance. sirâ€¦

5
00:00:57.265 --> 00:00:58.266
to prove myself.

6
00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:05.940
PERSONAL RECORD
PARK JIN-CHEOL

7
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:07.734
PERSONAL RECORD
SUNG HAN-SOO

8
00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:12.155
{\an8}A FEW HOURS EARLIER

9
00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.406
{\an8}What do you mean?

10
00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:19.162
What if we turned this
into a bigger problem? [scoffs]

11
00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:25.126
INTER-KOREAN GOVERNMENT TALKS

12
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.713
Hmm. Gosh. what's happening
that couldn't wait?

13
00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.383
{\an8}PRIME MINISTER
DELEGATION LEADER

14
00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.302
{\an8}Sir. you've been summoned by the DPRK.

15
00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.096
What?

16
00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.682
<i>What is going on?</i>

17
00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.602
Why do you suddenly
want to call off the negotiations?

18
00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.522
It is simply because
the Southern authorities

19
00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.650
are not yet prepared to engage
in meaningful dialogue.

20
00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.568
Excuse me?
What the hell are you talking about?

21
00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:54.781
You keep running your mouths
about peaceful talks and cooperation.

22
00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:58.243
all while you betray our Republic
and everything it stands for.

23
00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:01.579
-What did you say?
-We already know about Ri Eung Ryeong.

24
00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:06.084
the former Director General
of the Intelligence Bureau.

25
00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:09.921
Not only did you smuggle him
into your country.

26
00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:13.466
you also assigned the Republic's
most wanted criminal as his escort.

27
00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.848
I'm done talking to you.

28
00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:24.060
Unless you hand over those two
traitorous rats to us immediately.

29
00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.604
not only will we call off
these negotiations.

30
00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:28.898
but the relationship between
the North and the South

31
00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.192
will be changed beyond all recognition.

32
00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.369
Contact General Jang right away.

33
00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:42.787
I'm on it. sir.

34
00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.789
{\an8}EPISODE 9

35
00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.375
{\an8}ONCE A MARINE. ALWAYS A MARINE

36
00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:02.974
Your missionâ€¦

37
00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:05.393
has failed.

38
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.362
[delegation leader laughing]

39
00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.329
Watching the South's prime minister
back down like that

40
00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:26.039
was quite a sight.

41
00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:29.167
He tucked his tail between his legs.
[laughs]

42
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.794
Thanks to you. Comrade Ju.
everything went smoothly.

43
00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:36.466
I need your word
that I'll be the one to finish him.

44
00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.135
I always keep my promises. I assure you.

45
00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.221
Althoughâ€¦

46
00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:47.060
no one can be aware of this
except for you.

47
00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:50.021
Now that everything has been handled
through official channels.

48
00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:53.441
I must say.
taking 66 out on Southern soilâ€¦

49
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.610
is a burden we'd like to avoid.

50
00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.572
You don't have to worry.

51
00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:05.495
[chuckling]

52
00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:57.463
[Guk-cheol] <i>What do you mean by that?</i>

53
00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:01.968
Don't take Ri Eung Ryeong out until
we've secured intelligence on the missile.

54
00:05:02.051 --> 00:05:04.053
We've already failed the mission.

55
00:05:04.929 --> 00:05:06.681
Are you refusing to carry out

56
00:05:07.724 --> 00:05:10.560
-the orders of the PM?
-I am.

57
00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:14.355
66 and Ri Eung Ryeong
will be handed over to the North Koreans.

58
00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.736
<i>Thing is. if 66 keeps taking matters</i>
<i>into his own handsâ€¦</i>

59
00:05:20.862 --> 00:05:22.613
<i>that's got nothing to do with us.</i>

60
00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:26.659
<i>The only thing we can do now</i>
<i>is sit back and watch.</i>

61
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:37.337
<i>We all know</i>
<i>that man is willing to do anything</i>

62
00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.464
<i>just to see his daughter again.</i>

63
00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.556
AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

64
00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:51.350
Hey. so about Shit Cricketâ€¦

65
00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:53.686
He handcuffed him. right?

66
00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.229
Uh-huh.

67
00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.483
Even though he knows
they're useless against Kim.

68
00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:00.735
Mm-hmm.

69
00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.239
Then I guess he doesn't need our help.

70
00:06:10.286 --> 00:06:12.789
But won't it be hard for him
to make it back?

71
00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:15.500
This isn't just
some local street thug he's facing.

72
00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.050
Are you going?

73
00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.551
Are you?

74
00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:31.891
Huh?

75
00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:34.644
Look. Isn't that his phone there?

76
00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.855
-I guess he took mine instead.
-Huh?

77
00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:40.233
-Did he actually take yours?
-He must have taken it.

78
00:06:40.316 --> 00:06:42.110
Wow. he left that. He must be losing it.

79
00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:43.903
I better go get it. right?

80
00:06:43.986 --> 00:06:46.656
Of course you should.
A phone is really expensive.

81
00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.117
[sighs] I even owe on that thing.

82
00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.077
Then you'd better get going now!

83
00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.038
-That little punk. When I find himâ€¦
-Wait a second!

84
00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:55.915
Before we hit the roadâ€¦

85
00:06:57.708 --> 00:06:58.709
let's take one of these.

86
00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.420
-What are those?
-They're good for your joints.

87
00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:03.506
Seriously?
You've been keeping it all to yourself?

88
00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:04.841
I'm sharing them now.

89
00:07:10.805 --> 00:07:11.806
Let's go!

90
00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:14.225
Where'd you park?

91
00:07:15.226 --> 00:07:17.061
Whoa! Hey. what's with this car?

92
00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:19.480
This? They say it's the car of the future.

93
00:07:19.564 --> 00:07:22.400
"They say it's the car of the future."
Let's see what it's got.

94
00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.740
Hold on. Isn't the hero
supposed to be the one driving?

95
00:07:59.187 --> 00:08:00.646
[phone buzzing]

96
00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.941
66 will be handled by the other team.

97
00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.778
That's how
you get the job done effortlessly.

98
00:08:07.862 --> 00:08:10.823
<i>Now. report to both</i>
<i>the Southern side and the Party</i>

99
00:08:10.907 --> 00:08:14.076
<i>that Ri Eung Ryeong and 66 were executed.</i>

100
00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:15.620
Sir. I'm on it.

101
00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:41.896
Good riddance. enemy of the state.

102
00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:44.315
You shit stains.

103
00:08:44.398 --> 00:08:46.025
[grunting]

104
00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.392
I didn't know you were such a big deal.

105
00:09:20.351 --> 00:09:22.770
We didn't roll out the red carpet
for you last time.

106
00:09:23.312 --> 00:09:24.438
What a shame.

107
00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:26.566
I recall you said you'd turn yourself in.

108
00:09:27.984 --> 00:09:30.570
As it happens.
the parents' meeting is not over yet.

109
00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:37.785
So you're the rat
who joined forces with the North.

110
00:09:37.868 --> 00:09:39.328
The only rat here is you.

111
00:09:40.746 --> 00:09:42.832
The rat who betrayed his own country.

112
00:09:47.878 --> 00:09:49.714
We're alike in many ways.

113
00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:54.135
We're both willing to do anything
for our children.

114
00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.846
We're good fathers.

115
00:09:57.513 --> 00:09:58.598
Don't you agree?

116
00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.643
Didn't you say you'd get rid of me
for your daughter's sake?

117
00:10:04.645 --> 00:10:06.981
You should have known
I'd get rid of you for Hye-ri too.

118
00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:12.320
[tense music plays]

119
00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.042
I have plans for you.

120
00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:30.212
Put him in the trunk.

121
00:10:50.733 --> 00:10:51.734
[sighs]

122
00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:54.320
Comrade.

123
00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.076
Your car's really nice.

124
00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.459
Shh. shh. shhâ€¦

125
00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.211
Nighty-night.

126
00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.464
Hey. I didn't come here
to help you or anything.

127
00:11:15.758 --> 00:11:16.967
I came to bring you your phone.

128
00:11:17.051 --> 00:11:21.722
but the gunshots were so deafening.
I got dragged in. [chuckles]

129
00:11:21.806 --> 00:11:22.807
Thanks. man.

130
00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:26.727
So. what are you doing next?
Ri Eung Ryeong's likely dead.

131
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:29.563
I don't think he's dead.
They wanted him alive. you know?

132
00:11:29.647 --> 00:11:30.648
Really?

133
00:11:30.731 --> 00:11:33.192
This guy's really something else.
isn't he?

134
00:11:33.275 --> 00:11:35.194
Trying to get in bed with North Korea.

135
00:11:35.277 --> 00:11:36.987
He really doesn't think twice.

136
00:11:37.071 --> 00:11:38.489
You're the worst kind of jerk.

137
00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:42.451
Ri Eung Ryeong. Where is he now?

138
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:49.166
Shoot me.

139
00:11:50.418 --> 00:11:52.128
You wanna leave both our kids
without a father?

140
00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:53.838
Shoot.

141
00:11:53.921 --> 00:11:55.005
You actually did.

142
00:12:00.261 --> 00:12:01.262
Let's cut a deal.

143
00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.391
I know why you're after Ri Eung Ryeong.

144
00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:10.020
If you let me live.
I'll help you find the guy.

145
00:12:19.822 --> 00:12:20.948
Let's go.

146
00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:23.909
If you lie. you'll regret it.

147
00:12:26.787 --> 00:12:28.747
Nighty-night. Dream about me.

148
00:12:32.543 --> 00:12:33.544
Hey. Han-soo.

149
00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.421
Thanks for coming.

150
00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:41.218
We have to be around
when Min-ji walks down the aisle.

151
00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:47.391
Let's roll!

152
00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:55.316
[melancholic music playing]

153
00:13:40.361 --> 00:13:41.445
[agent] That's North Korean.

154
00:13:41.529 --> 00:13:43.531
SECURITY CHECK IN PROGRESS

155
00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:56.168
Let 'em through.

156
00:13:56.252 --> 00:13:57.878
Don't let your guard down.

157
00:14:05.094 --> 00:14:08.138
Geez. unbelievable.
What's with those guys?

158
00:14:08.222 --> 00:14:10.391
-[agent 1] Huh?
-[agent 2] Do they think we work for them?

159
00:14:10.474 --> 00:14:11.475
[agent 1] Just let it go.

160
00:14:12.101 --> 00:14:15.062
[agent 2] Don't you think our government
is trusting them too much?

161
00:14:15.145 --> 00:14:18.232
They won't even let us inside.
but they expect us to stand guard?

162
00:14:18.315 --> 00:14:19.441
That doesn't make sense.

163
00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:23.737
Did you forget? North Korea's
the world's most secretive country.

164
00:14:23.821 --> 00:14:26.240
And their delegation is right in there.

165
00:14:41.505 --> 00:14:43.799
JUHAK WELCOMES
THE NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION!

166
00:14:44.842 --> 00:14:47.303
Jong Il Peak 25
has just entered the lobby.

167
00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.436
Jong Il Peak 25 is in the service lift.

168
00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:01.817
Jong Il Peak 25 is on the fifth floor.

169
00:15:06.864 --> 00:15:09.658
Jong Il Peak 25
approaching the VIP reception.

170
00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:14.121
{\an8}<i>Jong Il Peak 25 is entering the VIP room.</i>

171
00:15:16.332 --> 00:15:19.418
-Should I report now. sir?
-Negative. I'll report to him myself.

172
00:15:57.289 --> 00:16:02.002
Ah. Comrade Director General.
you look like you're going through it.

173
00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:05.172
Have you been having a hard time
away from home?

174
00:16:05.255 --> 00:16:06.382
[scoffs]

175
00:16:07.716 --> 00:16:11.261
Quit stalling. Get it over with now.
What is it you're waiting for?

176
00:16:11.345 --> 00:16:14.765
Don't rush me. We can take our sweet time.

177
00:16:15.391 --> 00:16:16.392
[scoffs]

178
00:16:20.145 --> 00:16:23.524
It's in your best interest
to start revealing the missile intel

179
00:16:23.607 --> 00:16:25.442
that you've been sharing with the South.

180
00:16:25.943 --> 00:16:28.237
Oh. yeah. We have plenty to discuss.

181
00:16:30.197 --> 00:16:31.365
Now. fill the bathtub.

182
00:16:44.294 --> 00:16:45.295
How did it go?

183
00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:48.465
We saw a North Korean vehicle enter
a few minutes ago.

184
00:16:49.091 --> 00:16:52.052
They were carrying a fairly big bundle
of some sort.

185
00:16:53.095 --> 00:16:54.179
[whirring]

186
00:17:09.653 --> 00:17:10.738
[Kim] It's Ri Eung Ryeong.

187
00:17:11.447 --> 00:17:15.325
[Sang-a] <i>The MPs are stationed outside</i>
<i>and NIS agents are patrolling indoors.</i>

188
00:17:15.409 --> 00:17:18.162
<i>They can access areas</i>
<i>where South Korean employees work.</i>

189
00:17:18.245 --> 00:17:20.497
<i>such as the kitchen and laundry room.</i>

190
00:17:20.581 --> 00:17:23.584
But they're always under the eye
of the North Korean agents.

191
00:17:24.501 --> 00:17:25.836
They'll put up a fight.

192
00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:27.463
-Can I?
-Take a look.

193
00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:30.090
Which floor are the North Koreans on?

194
00:17:30.174 --> 00:17:31.842
The fourth and fifth floors.

195
00:17:31.925 --> 00:17:34.136
The head of the delegation
must be on the fifth floor.

196
00:17:34.762 --> 00:17:37.431
and the control room
must be on the fourth.

197
00:17:37.514 --> 00:17:39.349
That's their way of doing things.

198
00:17:40.225 --> 00:17:41.602
How are we going to get in?

199
00:17:50.861 --> 00:17:54.531
Hey. we need to get in that building
virtually unnoticed.

200
00:17:54.615 --> 00:17:56.450
Right. Fat chance he'll talk.

201
00:17:57.034 --> 00:17:58.494
The terms are very simple.

202
00:17:59.078 --> 00:18:02.289
If we get Ri Eung Ryeong with your help.
we'll let you live.

203
00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:04.583
If we fail. you die.

204
00:18:08.754 --> 00:18:10.881
On the resort.
there's an underground passage

205
00:18:10.964 --> 00:18:13.008
with a direct path
to the Chairman's office.

206
00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:15.844
It was built for emergencies.
so there's no CCTVs.

207
00:18:15.928 --> 00:18:18.680
Really? Wait a minute.
it can't be that easy.

208
00:18:19.348 --> 00:18:20.808
Hey. look at me when you talk.

209
00:18:20.891 --> 00:18:22.559
How do we get past the barricade?

210
00:18:23.977 --> 00:18:25.896
[sighs] I have clearance.

211
00:18:27.689 --> 00:18:28.774
I'm on VIP duty.

212
00:18:28.857 --> 00:18:31.401
Oh. it's simpler than I thought.

213
00:18:34.238 --> 00:18:38.784
Once we get to the office. with the CCTVs.
we'll be able to pinpoint his location.

214
00:18:39.743 --> 00:18:41.078
[Sang-a] But there's a problem.

215
00:18:41.662 --> 00:18:43.831
<i>They've shut down the existing CCTVs</i>

216
00:18:43.914 --> 00:18:45.999
<i>and are running the ones</i>
<i>they installed themselves</i>

217
00:18:46.083 --> 00:18:47.417
<i>upstairs in the control room.</i>

218
00:18:47.501 --> 00:18:50.712
We must first secure
the main control room. then.

219
00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.674
So you take the control room
and get his position.

220
00:18:53.757 --> 00:18:56.051
Then I'll focus
on getting him out of there.

221
00:18:56.135 --> 00:18:57.970
Then. while you get outâ€¦

222
00:18:58.053 --> 00:18:59.888
the two of us will keep 'em busy.

223
00:19:00.681 --> 00:19:02.307
-Me three.
-But waitâ€¦

224
00:19:03.058 --> 00:19:05.686
Simply getting him out
through the main entrance?

225
00:19:05.769 --> 00:19:08.272
I don't know. It won't be that easy. man.

226
00:19:09.356 --> 00:19:11.650
Yeah. you're right.
He'll get on the laundry truck

227
00:19:11.733 --> 00:19:13.318
at the loading dock on the first floor.

228
00:19:13.402 --> 00:19:14.444
Laundry truck?

229
00:19:14.987 --> 00:19:17.197
Since laundry is my thing now. I'm on it.

230
00:19:17.948 --> 00:19:20.534
<i>The laundry truck arrives at the dock</i>
<i>at 19:20 hours</i>

231
00:19:20.617 --> 00:19:22.411
and leaves at 19:30 hours.

232
00:19:22.494 --> 00:19:25.664
We'll only get ten minutes for the pickup.
Ten minutes. That's a small window.

233
00:19:25.747 --> 00:19:27.082
Ten minutes. then.

234
00:19:27.833 --> 00:19:31.378
We can pull him out to the loading dock.
We have to make it work.

235
00:19:31.461 --> 00:19:33.797
Ten minutes? Man. that plan really sucks.

236
00:19:34.506 --> 00:19:36.049
They communicate every three minutes.

237
00:19:36.133 --> 00:19:37.676
[groans] No way. dude.

238
00:19:37.759 --> 00:19:41.013
Why are you always getting so hung up
on how difficult it's gonna be?

239
00:19:41.096 --> 00:19:42.931
Why do you make it worse?
Are you scared?

240
00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:44.766
I'm not scared.
It's not like breaking boardsâ€¦

241
00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.268
[Han-soo] Why bring that up?

242
00:19:46.351 --> 00:19:47.895
-It's not gonna be as easy as you think.
-That's enough.

243
00:19:47.978 --> 00:19:49.813
I'll be on standby. just in case.

244
00:19:50.439 --> 00:19:54.443
We just need to go out
the way we came in.

245
00:19:56.737 --> 00:19:58.906
[Sang-a] We'll need
to pass the barricade first.

246
00:20:00.073 --> 00:20:02.367
Now let'sâ€¦ go get prepped for tonight.

247
00:20:02.451 --> 00:20:04.912
["Go! Go!" playing]

248
00:20:27.476 --> 00:20:29.228
Your wound. You should hide it.

249
00:20:33.315 --> 00:20:36.944
I think we're missing one.
The tranquilizer?

250
00:20:37.027 --> 00:20:38.654
Using both will give us the best chance.

251
00:20:38.737 --> 00:20:39.821
[grunts] That's enough.

252
00:20:39.905 --> 00:20:42.532
Oh. Hey. man. sorry about that.

253
00:20:45.327 --> 00:20:46.662
We're good. bro.

254
00:20:46.745 --> 00:20:49.122
I'll keep you updated in case
anything changes out here.

255
00:20:49.206 --> 00:20:51.208
Okay? Be careful. everyone.

256
00:20:51.291 --> 00:20:53.252
It took you four shots.

257
00:20:53.335 --> 00:20:55.128
[music continues]

258
00:21:00.175 --> 00:21:01.760
Ah. nice and warm in there?

259
00:21:03.011 --> 00:21:04.429
I hate playing rock-paper-scissors.

260
00:21:04.513 --> 00:21:07.224
Hmmâ€¦ You lost.

261
00:21:09.726 --> 00:21:11.228
-Cheaters!
-[Jin-cheol] Just have fun.

262
00:21:11.311 --> 00:21:12.145
[Han-soo] Shut up!

263
00:21:13.355 --> 00:21:14.856
Why does this always happen to me?

264
00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.400
[music continues]

265
00:21:27.536 --> 00:21:28.537
[music ends]

266
00:21:29.871 --> 00:21:30.706
AUTHORIZED VEHICLE

267
00:21:30.789 --> 00:21:33.292
Ju Gang-chan.
he's the chairman of the resort.

268
00:21:46.638 --> 00:21:47.973
Reason for your visit?

269
00:21:51.935 --> 00:21:53.895
To oversee the VIP arrangements.

270
00:21:55.439 --> 00:21:57.441
-Have you heard about this?
-No. sir.

271
00:22:03.113 --> 00:22:04.614
Roll down the back window. please.

272
00:22:13.999 --> 00:22:17.294
The Deputy Director of NS sent me.
You can verify it.

273
00:22:17.794 --> 00:22:19.004
[agent] Please wait a moment.

274
00:22:22.716 --> 00:22:25.469
Chairman Ju Gang-chan
came to oversee the VIP arrangements.

275
00:22:25.552 --> 00:22:27.554
Please verify that
with the Deputy Director.

276
00:22:33.769 --> 00:22:34.895
Yes. Got it.

277
00:22:37.314 --> 00:22:38.315
Here you go.

278
00:22:39.274 --> 00:22:40.275
Let them through.

279
00:22:40.859 --> 00:22:42.069
[agent 2] Open it now.

280
00:23:11.014 --> 00:23:12.766
[Han-soo groaning]

281
00:23:14.059 --> 00:23:15.268
Ow.

282
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:16.436
Oh. my knees.

283
00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:17.521
Ow. ow. ow!

284
00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:02.107
Hey. wait.

285
00:24:03.024 --> 00:24:06.444
Let's close it. Are you trying
to let everyone know we're here?

286
00:24:08.071 --> 00:24:09.531
NO ENTRY

287
00:24:23.712 --> 00:24:26.464
ACCESS RESTRICTED
ACCESS GRANTED

288
00:24:30.468 --> 00:24:31.303
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL

289
00:25:01.416 --> 00:25:03.627
Wow. it's fingerprint access.

290
00:25:04.336 --> 00:25:07.380
Was this place built only for you? Why?

291
00:25:07.464 --> 00:25:08.590
Just think it through.

292
00:25:09.090 --> 00:25:13.386
People with skeletons in the closet
always make sure they have an escape plan.

293
00:25:14.262 --> 00:25:15.430
-Ugh.
-Ugh.

294
00:25:15.513 --> 00:25:16.723
-Ugh.
-Ugh.

295
00:25:16.806 --> 00:25:17.807
Ugh.

296
00:25:19.976 --> 00:25:21.186
[elevator dings]

297
00:25:22.604 --> 00:25:23.605
Go.

298
00:25:29.110 --> 00:25:32.530
[Han-soo] Wow. this is the kind of door
you only see on TV.

299
00:25:32.614 --> 00:25:34.074
Why would someone build this?

300
00:25:34.157 --> 00:25:36.451
[Jin-Cheol] Because he has skeletons
in the closet.

301
00:25:36.534 --> 00:25:37.827
[Han-soo] Damn!

302
00:25:37.911 --> 00:25:41.498
[Jin-Cheol] Hey. guys. look. It's nice.
Want to switch offices? Huh?

303
00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:44.501
We need the blueprints.

304
00:25:47.671 --> 00:25:49.506
[Sang-a] Securing the station.
Three minutes.

305
00:25:49.589 --> 00:25:51.091
Mm-hmm. Two minutes.

306
00:25:51.174 --> 00:25:53.718
This is our only entrance. Right here.

307
00:25:53.802 --> 00:25:54.803
How much?

308
00:25:55.345 --> 00:25:59.432
To get to the loading dock.
we haveâ€¦ two minutes. I think.

309
00:26:00.100 --> 00:26:02.644
-Ms. Jung. you'll be all right?
-Yeah. I've got this.

310
00:26:03.561 --> 00:26:05.647
[Han-soo] I'll distract them
from the other side.

311
00:26:06.523 --> 00:26:09.150
All right. if everything
goes according to plan.

312
00:26:09.234 --> 00:26:12.070
we'll meet back here
at the Chairman's office.

313
00:26:13.738 --> 00:26:17.742
Put that gun away. will you?
That's not how you handle a civilian.

314
00:26:17.826 --> 00:26:19.202
[Han-soo] Seems fine.

315
00:26:20.328 --> 00:26:23.415
And even if I scream out loud.
no one outside this room can hear a thing.

316
00:26:23.498 --> 00:26:24.499
Really?

317
00:26:26.501 --> 00:26:27.502
Bang!

318
00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:29.796
[Jin-cheol laughs]

319
00:26:29.879 --> 00:26:31.965
-Everyone. let's get moving. Jin-Cheol.
-Oh. you're no fun.

320
00:26:35.510 --> 00:26:37.220
[clears throat] All right.

321
00:26:38.388 --> 00:26:40.682
Hi. hi. Hi. it's me.

322
00:26:42.183 --> 00:26:43.184
Send up room service.

323
00:26:43.935 --> 00:26:45.395
[Nam]<i> Everything's prepared.</i>

324
00:26:45.478 --> 00:26:46.896
[Jin-cheol] What can you send now?

325
00:26:51.401 --> 00:26:52.402
[knocking]

326
00:26:53.069 --> 00:26:54.070
[Jin-cheol] Yes.

327
00:26:55.822 --> 00:26:56.823
Come on in.

328
00:27:18.178 --> 00:27:19.637
Can you tell me your size?

329
00:27:19.721 --> 00:27:22.307
I'm a 3XL. sir.

330
00:27:22.390 --> 00:27:23.391
It's a little tight.

331
00:27:29.397 --> 00:27:31.024
I feel awkward in this chef's uniform.

332
00:27:32.192 --> 00:27:34.778
Once we find Ri Eung Ryeong.
we'll move in.

333
00:27:35.445 --> 00:27:37.280
-Please. be careful.
-You too.

334
00:27:37.364 --> 00:27:39.240
-[Jin-Cheol] How do I look?
-[Han-soo] You managed to squeeze into it.

335
00:27:39.324 --> 00:27:41.451
[Jin-Cheol] Yeah. I did.
Now you squeeze in there.

336
00:27:41.534 --> 00:27:44.412
-Oh. not again. I'm not a contortionist.
-Hurry.

337
00:27:44.496 --> 00:27:46.247
Why do you keep pushing me in tiny spaces?

338
00:27:46.331 --> 00:27:48.124
It's not like Mr. Park
can squeeze in there.

339
00:27:48.208 --> 00:27:50.126
What am I. origami paper? [grunts]

340
00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:51.753
That you can fold me at your will?

341
00:27:53.963 --> 00:27:55.840
-They're always making fun of me.
-Go.

342
00:27:55.924 --> 00:27:57.926
-[Jin-Cheol] Shut up.
-[Han-soo] Really?

343
00:28:08.103 --> 00:28:10.105
[upbeat music plays]

344
00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:24.452
[whimsical music plays]

345
00:28:26.871 --> 00:28:27.956
[Sang-a] Mwah!

346
00:28:29.457 --> 00:28:31.668
Damn. Are all the women in the South
that beautiful?

347
00:28:31.751 --> 00:28:33.211
Whoa. she is so pretty.

348
00:28:37.257 --> 00:28:38.675
[music ends]

349
00:28:41.761 --> 00:28:42.929
[Ho-won] Hi. guys.

350
00:28:43.012 --> 00:28:44.222
I'm here to collect the laundry.

351
00:28:44.305 --> 00:28:45.515
AUTHORIZED VEHICLE

352
00:28:50.937 --> 00:28:52.397
[agent 1] You may come in.

353
00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:54.691
-[agent 2] Let him through!
-[Ho-won] Thanks. have a good one.

354
00:28:59.320 --> 00:29:01.322
[doorbell rings]

355
00:29:09.873 --> 00:29:12.500
-Who is it?
-Room service. I have your order.

356
00:29:14.502 --> 00:29:15.795
Is it dinnertime already?

357
00:29:16.671 --> 00:29:17.881
It's a bit early. don't you think?

358
00:29:17.964 --> 00:29:19.924
Well. I'm hungry. so let's have dinner.

359
00:29:28.892 --> 00:29:30.226
[grunts]

360
00:29:34.230 --> 00:29:35.440
We make a pretty good team.

361
00:29:35.523 --> 00:29:37.025
My knees don't seem to agree.

362
00:29:37.692 --> 00:29:38.693
Control room secured.

363
00:29:51.581 --> 00:29:54.000
Oh. hey! Laundry guy! [chuckles]

364
00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:57.378
Don't open that one.
Start with the earlier footage.

365
00:29:57.462 --> 00:29:59.005
He's not here. but if you--

366
00:29:59.088 --> 00:30:00.924
-Why won't you listen?
-Hey. keep it down.

367
00:30:01.007 --> 00:30:02.592
We'll never find anything
if you keep rambling like that.

368
00:30:02.675 --> 00:30:04.010
Ugh. I'm really frustrated.

369
00:30:05.428 --> 00:30:06.721
Can we take a look at that one?

370
00:30:08.389 --> 00:30:09.641
Hey. Hey. hey. hey. hey. There.

371
00:30:10.809 --> 00:30:12.435
Oh. That's the bundle we saw.

372
00:30:13.603 --> 00:30:15.063
-Is he--
-Oh. let's follow them.

373
00:30:21.402 --> 00:30:22.403
Where is that?

374
00:30:22.487 --> 00:30:24.239
-Where is this?
-The suite on the fifth floor.

375
00:30:51.891 --> 00:30:52.976
[grunting]

376
00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:55.937
[water splashing]

377
00:30:56.855 --> 00:30:58.189
[delegation leader] That's enough.

378
00:30:59.399 --> 00:31:01.401
-[agent grunts]
-[Eung Ryeong groaning]

379
00:31:02.026 --> 00:31:03.570
[Eung Ryeong coughing]

380
00:31:06.197 --> 00:31:08.658
[Eung Ryeong] I've already told you
I kept my mouth shut.

381
00:31:08.741 --> 00:31:10.201
I didn't tell anyone!

382
00:31:11.119 --> 00:31:14.122
I haven't even met
with the Southern authorities yet!

383
00:31:16.416 --> 00:31:18.251
[delegation leader]
Of course. I suppose 66

384
00:31:18.334 --> 00:31:20.628
doesn't count
as a Southern authority after all.

385
00:31:21.296 --> 00:31:22.714
Hmm. Carry on.

386
00:31:25.842 --> 00:31:27.343
[agent 2] Comrade. sir!

387
00:31:29.429 --> 00:31:30.638
[Eung Ryeong choking]

388
00:31:32.807 --> 00:31:34.392
-Shit.
-What is it?

389
00:31:34.475 --> 00:31:37.103
It looks like the agents who went
to deal with 66 have gone missing.

390
00:31:37.186 --> 00:31:39.689
[delegation leader] Are you sure? 66â€¦

391
00:31:40.315 --> 00:31:41.357
I'm sure that he'll come here.

392
00:31:41.441 --> 00:31:45.486
There are Southern operatives outside too.
so take care of him without opening fire.

393
00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:47.780
-Understood. sir. You. follow me.
-Yes. sir.

394
00:31:53.870 --> 00:31:55.204
[agent 1] Shall we continue. sir?

395
00:31:56.497 --> 00:31:57.749
Bring him out now.

396
00:32:03.755 --> 00:32:06.507
[Jin-cheol] <i>Hey. Kim.</i>
<i>Kim. are you done yet?</i>

397
00:32:06.591 --> 00:32:08.635
Hey. do you really think
he can speak right now?

398
00:32:08.718 --> 00:32:11.429
I should be where he is.
since I'm the best of the three of us.

399
00:32:12.138 --> 00:32:13.473
There's not much time left.

400
00:32:14.390 --> 00:32:15.892
-[delegation leader] Sit down.
-Jeezâ€¦

401
00:32:15.975 --> 00:32:17.769
They're gonna catch on any second.

402
00:32:20.104 --> 00:32:22.398
-You two. wait outside.
-Sir?

403
00:32:23.066 --> 00:32:25.276
Did I make myself clear? Wait outside.

404
00:32:39.666 --> 00:32:41.960
Two agents have left.
but two are still waiting outside.

405
00:32:42.043 --> 00:32:43.044
Understood.

406
00:32:43.670 --> 00:32:45.880
[Eung Ryeong]
So. what are you planning now?

407
00:32:56.391 --> 00:32:58.518
I believe what you're saying. comrade.

408
00:32:58.601 --> 00:32:59.894
[clicks tongue]

409
00:32:59.978 --> 00:33:02.981
And trust me. the missile intel
couldn't matter less to me.

410
00:33:03.773 --> 00:33:07.735
That's why I'm trying to give you
a way out of this situation.

411
00:33:17.787 --> 00:33:21.624
The money you moved through Macau
to finance operations against the South.

412
00:33:23.418 --> 00:33:25.837
You converted eight million dollars
into casino chips

413
00:33:25.920 --> 00:33:28.840
and stashed them in a private vault
at the Fanta Casino.

414
00:33:29.757 --> 00:33:31.926
Just hand over the vault access card.

415
00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:36.014
and I'll personally arrange for you
to stow away on a ship to another country.

416
00:33:41.144 --> 00:33:42.353
[chuckles]

417
00:33:46.816 --> 00:33:48.860
So my hunch was right after all.

418
00:33:49.777 --> 00:33:51.738
That's the reason you kept me alive

419
00:33:51.821 --> 00:33:55.074
despite the order they gave
to get rid of me.

420
00:33:57.035 --> 00:33:59.954
The access card. Where do I find it?

421
00:34:00.038 --> 00:34:02.290
If I turn the card over too soon.

422
00:34:02.373 --> 00:34:05.251
I'd be losing my only leverage
in this negotiation.

423
00:34:06.127 --> 00:34:09.380
I knew I had to be prepared
for this kind of situation.

424
00:34:09.464 --> 00:34:13.926
so before coming down to the South.
I went to China and hid it.

425
00:34:14.010 --> 00:34:15.553
Don't try to fool me!

426
00:34:16.721 --> 00:34:18.306
This isn't a negotiation.

427
00:34:18.890 --> 00:34:21.768
I can kill you right now
with official authorization.

428
00:34:23.102 --> 00:34:27.732
I'm giving you one last chance.
Tell me now. Where's the access card?

429
00:34:34.155 --> 00:34:35.406
[laughs]

430
00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:40.912
I knew you'd come for me.
66 never disappoints.

431
00:34:41.662 --> 00:34:43.122
66. you'reâ€¦ [coughs]

432
00:34:43.206 --> 00:34:46.375
â€¦the finest warrior of North Korea.

433
00:34:46.918 --> 00:34:48.127
-I think that--
-Shut it.

434
00:34:49.003 --> 00:34:50.171
If you want to live.

435
00:34:50.797 --> 00:34:51.714
[chuckles]

436
00:34:54.801 --> 00:34:55.802
I got the package.

437
00:34:59.514 --> 00:35:00.932
<i>They won't risk shooting.</i>

438
00:35:01.808 --> 00:35:04.185
Okay. No need to make a mess here.

439
00:35:04.268 --> 00:35:07.146
We don't have much time.
Let's get started. Let's go. Chef.

440
00:35:09.816 --> 00:35:11.651
Don't forget to report in.

441
00:35:11.734 --> 00:35:14.445
Whew. that's quite a load today. Whew!

442
00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:17.865
[exhales. grunts]

443
00:35:19.158 --> 00:35:20.493
[groans]

444
00:35:21.077 --> 00:35:22.120
Ah!

445
00:35:34.173 --> 00:35:37.885
Laundry truck ready at the loading dock.
Come on. please hurry.

446
00:35:38.553 --> 00:35:40.721
Hey! You guys from up north!

447
00:35:41.764 --> 00:35:43.391
Hey. your security's been breached!

448
00:35:43.474 --> 00:35:46.060
Getting in was way too easy. man.

449
00:35:46.144 --> 00:35:49.063
We're here. so you're screwed. Get ready.

450
00:35:49.689 --> 00:35:50.690
[Han-soo] Hey. Jin-cheol.

451
00:35:54.026 --> 00:35:55.027
Rock and roll!

452
00:35:58.698 --> 00:35:59.699
[Jin-cheol] Ahâ€¦

453
00:36:14.797 --> 00:36:16.132
-[groans]
-[buzzer sounds]

454
00:36:16.591 --> 00:36:17.592
Youâ€¦

455
00:36:24.432 --> 00:36:27.852
Don't forget. Each one of us
is taking 15. Keep track.

456
00:36:27.935 --> 00:36:29.937
[Jin-cheol. agent screaming]

457
00:36:38.279 --> 00:36:40.823
-Come on. demo team.
-I'll show you demo team.

458
00:36:48.289 --> 00:36:51.500
[sighs] Mr. Kim.
we haven't secured the route yet.

459
00:36:51.584 --> 00:36:53.002
The two agents are still there.

460
00:37:01.886 --> 00:37:04.347
Surveillance. Any unusual activity?

461
00:37:05.223 --> 00:37:06.682
Surveillance. Surveillance!

462
00:37:08.059 --> 00:37:09.435
What are they doing?

463
00:37:11.812 --> 00:37:12.813
Move. now!

464
00:37:15.024 --> 00:37:17.109
Mr. Kim. they know we're here.

465
00:37:17.860 --> 00:37:21.239
-They'll be there any second. Get out.
-<i>What about you?</i>

466
00:37:21.322 --> 00:37:22.657
We don't have time to waste.

467
00:37:23.366 --> 00:37:24.742
We'll move out. One minute.

468
00:38:01.112 --> 00:38:02.321
Go check there!

469
00:38:04.824 --> 00:38:05.992
[grunts]

470
00:38:08.869 --> 00:38:11.872
He's already at the resort.
That motherfucker.

471
00:38:13.207 --> 00:38:14.375
What is all this?

472
00:38:15.167 --> 00:38:17.712
Three of them jumped us.
They suddenly showed up.

473
00:38:17.795 --> 00:38:19.130
There's three of them. huh?

474
00:38:20.047 --> 00:38:23.134
Secure our radio communications
and activate the jamming device. Now!

475
00:38:23.217 --> 00:38:24.218
Yes. sir!

476
00:38:26.429 --> 00:38:29.724
What are you doing?
Get the cameras back up! Now!

477
00:38:29.807 --> 00:38:30.808
I'm on it. sir.

478
00:38:39.025 --> 00:38:39.859
ACTIVATION READY

479
00:38:43.446 --> 00:38:45.656
We need to cut off
all their communications.

480
00:38:47.408 --> 00:38:49.410
Hey. Kim. are you there?
Do you still need more time--

481
00:38:49.493 --> 00:38:51.120
-[feedback]
-[all groaning]

482
00:38:57.543 --> 00:38:58.627
[groans]

483
00:38:59.545 --> 00:39:00.921
What's going on?

484
00:39:04.050 --> 00:39:06.886
What are you planning to do
now that we're cut off?

485
00:39:12.516 --> 00:39:14.935
Hey. you guys know how to use a jammer?

486
00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:16.395
{\an8}A SIGNAL JAMMING DEVICE
USED TO DISRUPT GPS OR RADAR

487
00:39:16.479 --> 00:39:17.938
{\an8}That's how they start their attacks.

488
00:39:18.022 --> 00:39:20.691
What the hell are you saying?
We've been under attack all night long.

489
00:39:20.775 --> 00:39:22.777
[sighs] Come on.
we can end this right here.

490
00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.236
Feels like the whole North is here.

491
00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:26.364
-Yeah. bring it on!
-Just go away!

492
00:39:26.989 --> 00:39:27.990
